  "problem": "Given that the random variables \n\n$$\n{X}_{1}∼N(2,2),\\,{X}_{2}∼N(1,{3}^{2}),\\,{X}_{3}∼N(3,8)\n$$\n\nare mutually independent and $Y=4{X}_{1}+3{X}_{2}-{X}_{3},$ calculate $P(5<Y<10).$ \n\n*Hint: A table of values of $Φ(z)$ for different values of $z$ is given below, where $Φ(z)$ is the cumulative distribution function for the standard normal distribution. *\n\n<table align=\"center\">\n\n<tbody><tr>\n<th>\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"5\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr> <th width=\"25%\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$z$</th><th bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$\\,0.06\\,$</th><th bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$\\,0.07\\,$</th><th bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$\\,0.08\\,$</th>\n</tr><tr> <th bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$\\,-0.6\\,$</th><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.2546\\,$ </td><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.2514\\,$ </td><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.2483\\,$ </td></tr>\n<tr> <th bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$\\,-0.4\\,$</th><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.3228\\,$ </td><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.3192\\,$ </td><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.3156\\,$ </td></tr>\n<tr> <th bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$\\,-0.2\\,$</th><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.3974\\,$ </td><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.3936\\,$ </td><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.3897\\,$ </td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n</th>\n\n<th width=\"5%\"></th>\n\n<th>\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"5\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr> <th width=\"25%\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$z$</th><th bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$\\,0.07\\,$</th><th bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$\\,0.08\\,$</th><th bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$\\,0.09\\,$</th>\n</tr><tr> <th bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$\\,0.1\\,$</th><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.5675\\,$ </td><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.5714\\,$ </td><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.5753\\,$ </td></tr>\n<tr> <th bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$\\,0.3\\,$</th><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.6443\\,$ </td